---
import { existsSync } from "node:fs";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";

const portraitPath = "/profile/agustin-vignolo-portrait.jpg";
const portraitAvailable = existsSync(
  new URL("../../public/profile/agustin-vignolo-portrait.jpg", import.meta.url),
);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Agustín Vignolo: backend and data engineer in Montevideo, what he is looking for, and why he writes."
>
  <section class="page-section page-header page-header-essay about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>{site.author}</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        I'm a backend and data engineer in Montevideo, Uruguay. I like the
        part of software where the numbers have to add up: pipelines,
        reconciliation, multi-tenant data, and the checks that prove a system
        is doing what it claims.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>Get in touch</a>
        <a class="button" href="/resume/">View resume</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="about-portrait-panel" aria-label="Portrait">
      <button
        class="about-flip-button"
        type="button"
        data-flip-card
        data-flipped="true"
        aria-pressed="true"
        aria-label="Show Goatveloper mark"
      >
        <span class="about-flip-glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="about-flip-card">
          <span class="about-flip-face about-flip-front" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="theme-logo theme-logo-themed about-flip-logo">
              <img
                class="theme-logo-asset theme-logo-light"
                src="/brand/goatveloper-full-dark.png"
                width="2048"
                height="2048"
                alt=""
                loading="eager"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <img
                class="theme-logo-asset theme-logo-dark"
                src="/brand/goatveloper-full-light.png"
                width="2048"
                height="2048"
                alt=""
                loading="eager"
                decoding="async"
              />
            </span>
          </span>

          <span class="about-flip-face about-flip-back" aria-hidden="true">
            {
              portraitAvailable ? (
                <img
                  class="about-portrait-image"
                  src={portraitPath}
                  alt=""
                  width="1024"
                  height="1024"
                  loading="eager"
                  decoding="async"
                />
              ) : (
                <span class="about-portrait-placeholder">
                  <span>AVS</span>
                </span>
              )
            }
          </span>
        </span>

        <span class="about-flip-prompt" data-flip-card-prompt>
          Show Goatveloper
        </span>
      </button>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section essay-stack">
    <div class="essay-block" data-bleed-line>
      <h2>How I got here</h2>
      <p>
        I started on Node.js and MongoDB as an intern, then spent two years at
        Seta Workshop owning a multi-tenant Rails platform end to end, from raw
        SQL reports to a Rails 5 to 7.1 upgrade. At Advisor Engine I moved to
        the JVM side of a wealth-management platform serving large US
        custodians. There I worked on Spring Batch and Spark pipelines and
        built the reconciliation, validation and data-quality checks around
        them. In parallel I was technical lead at URadar, a multi-tenant
        TypeScript platform with LangGraph agents running on AWS.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also finishing my BSc in Computer Systems Engineering at ORT
        University (Dec 2026), and I run Sistaller, a SaaS for automotive
        workshops that is in production with its first customer.
      </p>
      <figure class="about-figure">
        <img
          src="/profile/agustin-vignolo-thesis-presentation.jpg"
          alt="Agustín Vignolo presenting his degree project at a lectern."
          width="746"
          height="780"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>Presenting my degree project at ORT University.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="essay-block essay-block-split" data-bleed-line>
      <section>
        <h2>What I'm looking for</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Remote backend or data engineering roles.</li>
          <li>Data-intensive products, fintech first.</li>
          <li>Teams that care about correctness, tests and operability.</li>
          <li>Good overlap with US hours from Montevideo (UTC-3).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How I work</h2>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Make invariants explicit, then check them automatically.</li>
          <li>Design jobs to be restartable and idempotent from day one.</li>
          <li>Put CI around anything that matters, even old code.</li>
          <li>Write down decisions so the next person can follow them.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="essay-block" data-bleed-line>
      <h2>Why I write</h2>
      <p>
        Writing is how I check that I actually understand what I built. The
        notes here come from real work: what broke, what I changed, and the
        tradeoffs I would make again. Some of it should be useful to other
        engineers too.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're hiring or want to talk about any of it, email me at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>, or
        find me on <a href={site.contact.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        and <a href={site.contact.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
